    "doc_type": "journal_article",
    "title": "Manipulation-Proof Machine Learning",
    "summary": "This paper addresses the problem of strategic behavior in machine learning, where individuals manipulate their actions to influence algorithmic decisions. The authors develop a 'strategy-robust' estimator that incorporates a game-theoretic model of manipulation costs to produce stable decision rules, even under full transparency. They validate this approach through a field experiment in Kenya, demonstrating that their method outperforms standard machine learning algorithms in predictive accuracy when agents are incentivized to game the system.",
