    "title": "Causal Inference from Hypothetical Evaluations",
    "summary": "This paper proposes a method for causal inference that combines observational data on real choices with hypothetical evaluations to estimate treatment effects. The authors demonstrate that this approach can recover unbiased treatment effects in settings where standard methods fail, such as when treatment is endogenous or unobserved, and provide proof of concept through laboratory and field experiments.",
